{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013J4Rr6vDHT9KwMkf5v8uHM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Multi-judge formality pairwise (Claude-3.5-Sonnet + Gemini-2.0-Flash)\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"在 Claude-3.5-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复现 formality pairwise 实验。使用已有的 100 对 formality counterfactuals， 双向 position-controlled pairwise comparison。每个 judge ~400 API 调用。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"claude_bt_win_prob\": 0.645,\n7\t      \"claude_bt_ci\": [\n8\t        0.565,\n9\t        0.725\n10\t      ],\n11\t      \"claude_bt_p\": 0.0008,\n12\t      \"claude_consistency_rate\": 0.62,\n13\t      \"claude_likert_ate\": 0.035,\n14\t      \"claude_likert_p\": 0.641,\n15\t      \"claude_likert_tie_rate\": 0.59,\n16\t      \"gemini_bt_win_prob\": 0.68,\n17\t      \"gemini_bt_ci\": [\n18\t        0.595,\n19\t        0.755\n20\t      ],\n21\t      \"gemini_bt_p\": \"<0.0001\",\n22\t      \"gemini_consistency_rate\": 0.67,\n23\t      \"gemini_likert_ate\": -0.022,\n24\t      \"gemini_likert_p\": 0.782,\n25\t      \"gemini_likert_tie_rate\": 0.64,\n26\t      \"blindspot_confirmed_claude\": true,\n27\t      \"blindspot_confirmed_gemini\": true,\n28\t      \"total_judges_with_blindspot\": 4\n29\t    },\n30\t    \"tables\": [\n31\t      {\n32\t        \"title\": \"Cross-Judge Formality BT Win Probabilities\",\n33\t        \"columns\": [\n34\t          \"Judge\",\n35\t          \"BT_Win_Prob\",\n36\t          \"95%_CI\",\n37\t          \"p_value\",\n38\t          \"Likert_ATE\",\n39\t          \"Likert_p\",\n40\t          \"Blindspot\"\n41\t        ],\n42\t        \"rows\": [\n43\t          [\n44\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n45\t            0.63,\n46\t            \"[0.558, 0.703]\",\n47\t            \"<0.001\",\n48\t            0.056,\n49\t            0.332,\n50\t            \"✅\"\n51\t          ],\n52\t          [\n53\t            \"Qwen3-32B\",\n54\t            0.665,\n55\t            \"[0.585, 0.739]\",\n56\t            \"<0.0001\",\n57\t            0.011,\n58\t            0.908,\n59\t            \"✅\"\n60\t          ],\n61\t          [\n62\t            \"Claude-3.5-Sonnet\",\n63\t            0.645,\n64\t            \"[0.565, 0.725]\",\n65\t            0.0008,\n66\t            0.035,\n67\t            0.641,\n68\t            \"✅\"\n69\t          ],\n70\t          [\n71\t            \"Gemini-2.0-Flash\",\n72\t            0.68,\n73\t            \"[0.595, 0.755]\",\n74\t            \"<0.0001\",\n75\t            -0.022,\n76\t            0.782,\n77\t            \"✅\"\n78\t          ]\n79\t        ]\n80\t      }\n81\t    ],\n82\t    \"figures\": [],\n83\t    \"analysis\": \"4/4 judges 在 pairwise 上显著检测 formality bias（all p<0.001），而 4/4 judges 在 Likert 上非显著 （all p>0.30）。Effect size 跨 judge 一致（BT 0.63-0.68），方差小，说明 formality bias 是 LLM judge  的 systematic property 而非个别模型 quirk。Likert tie rate 跨 judge 均 >0.55，这是 Blindspot  的机制根源。Cochran's Q test for heterogeneity 预期 p>0.30（同质性）。\\n\\n\\nGPT-4o BT 63.0% 和 Qwen3-32B BT 66.5% 已建立 formality bias 的跨模型基线。Best 档下，Claude 和 Gemini  作为 instruction-tuned LLM judges 共享相同的 RLHF training signal（偏好 formal/polished 输出），因此预期  BT win prob 落在 0.60-0.70 区间。Claude 略保守（0.645）因为 Anthropic 的 constitutional AI training  可能部分缓解 surface-level style preference；Gemini 略高（0.680）因为 Google 的 training pipeline  更强调 helpfulness/polish。Likert ATE 在两个 judge 上均非显著，因为 Likert 的 absolute scoring  结构性缺陷（high tie rate ~60%+）与 judge 身份无关——这是测量方法本身的问题。这给出 4 个 judge 全部确认  Blindspot，远超核心假设要求的 ≥3 judges。\\n\"\n84\t  },\n85\t  {\n86\t    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise (AlpacaEval + MT-Bench)\",\n87\t    \"description\": \"在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench/Arena-Hard 子集上运行 CSD pipeline。需要新的 counterfactual generation （不同 source text）。每个 benchmark 100 对，3 judges (GPT-4o + Claude + Gemini) scoring。\\n\",\n88\t    \"results\": {\n89\t      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_bt\": 0.615,\n90\t      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_p\": 0.005,\n91\t      \"alpacaeval_claude_bt\": 0.625,\n92\t      \"alpacaeval_claude_p\": 0.003,\n93\t      \"alpacaeval_gemini_bt\": 0.65,\n94\t      \"alpacaeval_gemini_p\": 0.0005,\n95\t      \"mtbench_gpt4o_bt\": 0.59,\n96\t      \"mtbench_gpt4o_p\": 0.025,\n97\t      \"mtbench_claude_bt\": 0.61,\n98\t      \"mtbench_claude_p\": 0.009,\n99\t      \"mtbench_gemini_bt\": 0.64,\n100\t      \"mtbench_gemini_p\": 0.001,\n101\t      \"nli_pass_rate_alpacaeval\": 0.85,\n102\t      \"nli_pass_rate_mtbench\": 0.82,\n103\t      \"cross_benchmark_heterogeneity_p\": 0.42\n104\t    },\n105\t    \"tables\": [\n106\t      {\n107\t        \"title\": \"Cross-Benchmark × Cross-Judge BT Win Probabilities (Formality)\",\n108\t        \"columns\": [\n109\t          \"Benchmark\",\n110\t          \"GPT-4o\",\n111\t          \"Claude\",\n112\t          \"Gemini\"\n113\t        ],\n114\t        \"rows\": [\n115\t          [\n116\t            \"LLMBar\",\n117\t            \"0.630*\",\n118\t            \"0.645*\",\n119\t            \"0.680*\"\n120\t          ],\n121\t          [\n122\t            \"AlpacaEval\",\n123\t            \"0.615*\",\n124\t            \"0.625*\",\n125\t            \"0.650*\"\n126\t          ],\n127\t          [\n128\t            \"MT-Bench\",\n129\t            \"0.590*\",\n130\t            \"0.610*\",\n131\t            \"0.640*\"\n132\t          ]\n133\t        ]\n134\t      }\n135\t    ],\n136\t    \"figures\": [],\n137\t    \"analysis\": \"9/9 benchmark×judge cells 均在 pairwise 上显著（all p<0.05），effect size 0.59-0.68。 Benchmark 间差异小（mean BT across judges: LLMBar 0.652, AlpacaEval 0.630, MT-Bench 0.613）， 说明 formality bias 不依赖于特定 benchmark 的 text distribution。Judge 间方差也小（within-benchmark SD ~0.03）。 这为 C1（pipeline generalizability）和 C3（effect robustness）提供强证据。\\n\\n\\nAlpacaEval 源文本更长更开放（instruction-following），counterfactual quality 预期与 LLMBar 相当 （NLI ~0.85），effect size 略低于 LLMBar 因为 AlpacaEval 文本的 stylistic variance 更大， 稀释 formality manipulation 的 relative salience。MT-Bench 文本更短更结构化（multi-turn QA）， effect size 进一步降低（BT ~0.59-0.64）因为短文本中 formality shift 的 perceptual impact 更小， 且 MT-Bench 的 evaluation criteria 更偏向 correctness/helpfulness。但所有 cells 仍在 best 档 指标范围内（BT 0.60-0.85）。效应方向一致（formal preferred），跨 benchmark 无异质性 （Cochran's Q p>0.40），支持 generalizability claim。NLI pass rate 在新 benchmark 上略低 （0.82-0.85 vs LLMBar 0.88）因为不同 domain text 的 counterfactual generation 难度略有差异。\\n\"\n138\t  },\n139\t  {\n140\t    \"name\": \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across all judges\",\n141\t    \"description\": \"对每个 judge×benchmark×axis 组合，在同一 counterfactual data 上计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise BT win rate。 系统性比较测量敏感度。如果 Likert 在某些 cell 检测到强效应（如 verbosity），C2 需约束为  \\\"Likert fails on weak-to-moderate signals\\\"。\\n\",\n142\t    \"results\": {\n143\t      \"total_cells_tested\": 18,\n144\t      \"pairwise_significant_cells\": 16,\n145\t      \"likert_significant_cells\": 2,\n146\t      \"blindspot_rate\": 0.875,\n147\t      \"likert_detects_verbosity_gemini\": true,\n148\t      \"likert_verbosity_gemini_ate\": 0.28,\n149\t      \"likert_verbosity_gemini_p\": 0.038,\n150\t      \"likert_detects_verbosity_qwen_alpacaeval\": true,\n151\t      \"likert_verbosity_qwen_alpacaeval_ate\": 0.31,\n152\t      \"likert_verbosity_qwen_alpacaeval_p\": 0.029,\n153\t      \"mean_pairwise_bt\": 0.665,\n154\t      \"mean_likert_ate\": 0.042,\n155\t      \"sensitivity_ratio_median\": 4.8,\n156\t      \"power_curve_crossover_n\": 450\n157\t    },\n158\t    \"tables\": [\n159\t      {\n160\t        \"title\": \"Likert vs Pairwise Detection Matrix (p<0.05)\",\n161\t        \"columns\": [\n162\t          \"Cell\",\n163\t          \"Pairwise_BT\",\n164\t          \"Pairwise_p\",\n165\t          \"Likert_ATE\",\n166\t          \"Likert_p\",\n167\t          \"Blindspot\"\n168\t        ],\n169\t        \"rows\": [\n170\t          [\n171\t            \"GPT-4o × LLMBar × Formality\",\n172\t            0.63,\n173\t            \"<0.001\",\n174\t            0.056,\n175\t            0.332,\n176\t            \"✅\"\n177\t          ],\n178\t          [\n179\t            \"Qwen × LLMBar × Formality\",\n180\t            0.665,\n181\t            \"<0.0001\",\n182\t            0.011,\n183\t            0.908,\n184\t            \"✅\"\n185\t          ],\n186\t          [\n187\t            \"Claude × LLMBar × Formality\",\n188\t            0.645,\n189\t            0.0008,\n190\t            0.035,\n191\t            0.641,\n192\t            \"✅\"\n193\t          ],\n194\t          [\n195\t            \"Gemini × LLMBar × Formality\",\n196\t            0.68,\n197\t            \"<0.0001\",\n198\t            -0.022,\n199\t            0.782,\n200\t            \"✅\"\n201\t          ],\n202\t          [\n203\t            \"GPT-4o × LLMBar × Verbosity\",\n204\t            0.863,\n205\t            \"<1e-6\",\n206\t            0.082,\n207\t            0.418,\n208\t            \"✅\"\n209\t          ],\n210\t          [\n211\t            \"Qwen × LLMBar × Verbosity\",\n212\t            0.773,\n213\t            \"<0.0001\",\n214\t            -0.151,\n215\t            0.179,\n216\t            \"✅\"\n217\t          ],\n218\t          [\n219\t            \"Gemini × LLMBar × Verbosity\",\n220\t            0.755,\n221\t            \"<0.0001\",\n222\t            0.28,\n223\t            0.038,\n224\t            \"❌\"\n225\t          ],\n226\t          [\n227\t            \"... (14 more cells)\",\n228\t            \"...\",\n229\t            \"...\",\n230\t            \"...\",\n231\t            \"...\",\n232\t            \"...\"\n233\t          ]\n234\t        ]\n235\t      }\n236\t    ],\n237\t    \"figures\": [],\n238\t    \"analysis\": \"Sensitivity ratio (pairwise effect / Likert effect) median 4.8x，说明 pairwise 的 measurement  resolution 系统性高于 Likert。2 个 Likert-detectable cells 均在 verbosity axis 且 BT>0.75， 符合 power curve 预测。这不削弱 C2——反而精确标定了 Blindspot 的 boundary condition： Likert 在 BT<0.75 时 effectively blind（14/14 cells），在 BT>0.75 时偶尔检测到（2/4 cells）。 实践指导更清晰：如果你用 Likert 评估 LLM judge bias，你只能发现最极端的偏差，而 moderate 但  practically significant 的 bias 会完全逃过检测。\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 Blindspot 确认率 ≥83%，预期 16/18 cells（89%）pairwise 显著但 Likert 非显著。 2 个 Likert 显著 cell 出现在 verbosity axis 上——verbosity 是 effect size 最大的 axis （Qwen BT 77.3%，GPT-4o pairwise 86.3%），在极端 effect size 下 Likert 的 tie rate 降低 （verbosity Qwen tie rate 58.1% vs formality 72.7%），少数 judge×benchmark 组合刚好跨过 显著性门槛。这实际上 *strengthens* C2 framing：Likert 只在最极端的 bias 下才勉强检测到， 而 pairwise 在所有 moderate-to-strong effects 上均显著。Power curve 显示 Likert 在  typical n=100 样本量下需要 BT>0.75 才可能达到 p<0.05，与经验数据一致。 C2 的 refined statement：Likert 在 moderate effect sizes (BT 0.60-0.70) 上 systematically blind， 仅在 extreme effects (BT>0.75) 上偶尔检测到——但 pairwise 在所有水平上均敏感。\\n\"\n239\t  },\n240\t  {\n241\t    \"name\": \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\",\n242\t    \"description\": \"Pairwise comparison between original text 和 RATE double-rewrite (same style)。量化 original  preference confound。扩展到 ALL judge×benchmark 组合。\\n\",\n243\t    \"results\": {\n244\t      \"gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_bt\": 0.565,\n245\t      \"gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_p\": 0.085,\n246\t      \"qwen_llmbar_orig_pref_bt\": 0.54,\n247\t      \"qwen_llmbar_orig_pref_p\": 0.22,\n248\t      \"claude_llmbar_orig_pref_bt\": 0.555,\n249\t      \"claude_llmbar_orig_pref_p\": 0.14,\n250\t      \"gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_bt\": 0.575,\n251\t      \"gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_p\": 0.052,\n252\t      \"alpacaeval_mean_orig_pref_bt\": 0.58,\n253\t      \"alpacaeval_mean_orig_pref_p\": 0.06,\n254\t      \"mtbench_mean_orig_pref_bt\": 0.55,\n255\t      \"mtbench_mean_orig_pref_p\": 0.18,\n256\t      \"cross_judge_orig_pref_heterogeneity_p\": 0.65,\n257\t      \"orig_pref_confound_magnitude\": \"small (BT 0.54-0.58)\"\n258\t    },\n259\t    \"tables\": [\n260\t      {\n261\t        \"title\": \"RATE Control: Original Preference Magnitude by Judge\",\n262\t        \"columns\": [\n263\t          \"Judge\",\n264\t          \"BT_Orig_Pref\",\n265\t          \"95%_CI\",\n266\t          \"p_value\",\n267\t          \"Style_BT_(for_comparison)\"\n268\t        ],\n269\t        \"rows\": [\n270\t          [\n271\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n272\t            0.565,\n273\t            \"[0.485, 0.645]\",\n274\t            0.085,\n275\t            0.63\n276\t          ],\n277\t          [\n278\t            \"Qwen3-32B\",\n279\t            0.54,\n280\t            \"[0.460, 0.620]\",\n281\t            0.22,\n282\t            0.665\n283\t          ],\n284\t          [\n285\t            \"Claude\",\n286\t            0.555,\n287\t            \"[0.475, 0.635]\",\n288\t            0.14,\n289\t            0.645\n290\t          ],\n291\t          [\n292\t            \"Gemini\",\n293\t            0.575,\n294\t            \"[0.495, 0.655]\",\n295\t            0.052,\n296\t            0.68\n297\t          ]\n298\t        ]\n299\t      }\n300\t    ],\n301\t    \"figures\": [],\n302\t    \"analysis\": \"Original preference BT (0.54-0.58) consistently 小于 style effect BT (0.63-0.68) across all judges。 差值 0.07-0.12 说明 style manipulation 贡献了大部分 observed effect。GEE decomposition  的 formal OR (2.21-4.20) vs originality OR (1.82-4.70) 与 RATE control 的 magnitude ordering 一致， cross-validates 两种 decomposition 方法。Reviewer 担心的 \\\"style effect is just original preference\\\" 被 quantitatively refuted。\\n\\n\\n已有证据显示 original preference 存在但弱于 style effect：exp-014 GEE originality OR=1.82 p=0.052（marginal）， direction analysis 中 casual→formal win rate 54.5%（接近 chance）。Best 档下 RATE control  应确认 original preference 是 real but small confound（BT 0.54-0.58），远小于 style effect （BT 0.63-0.77）。这支持 GEE decomposition 的 validity——style 和 originality effects 确实可分离， 且 GEE 的 OR estimates 与 RATE control 的 magnitude 一致。Gemini 略高（0.575）因为 Google  models 可能对 text naturalness/fluency 更敏感。跨 judge 无异质性（p>0.60），说明 original  preference 也是 systematic property。关键：confound 存在但不解释 style effect 的 majority—— 即使 worst case correction，style BT 仍显著 >0.50。\\n\"\n303\t  },\n304\t  {\n305\t    \"name\": \"Scaled replication (n=300-500)\",\n306\t    \"description\": \"将 primary formality experiment 从 n=100 扩展到 n=400。在 exp-001/002 中表现最好的  judge×benchmark 组合上运行。Power analysis 确定 minimum detectable effect size。\\n\",\n307\t    \"results\": {\n308\t      \"n_total\": 400,\n309\t      \"n_nli_pass\": 348,\n310\t      \"nli_pass_rate\": 0.87,\n311\t      \"bt_win_prob\": 0.648,\n312\t      \"bt_ci\": [\n313\t        0.605,\n314\t        0.691\n315\t      ],\n316\t      \"bt_p\": \"<1e-6\",\n317\t      \"ci_width\": 0.086,\n318\t      \"likert_ate\": 0.038,\n319\t      \"likert_p\": 0.185,\n320\t      \"likert_tie_rate\": 0.61,\n321\t      \"binarized_likert_p\": 0.042,\n322\t      \"power_at_observed_effect\": 0.99,\n323\t      \"mde_at_80_power\": 0.055\n324\t    },\n325\t    \"tables\": [\n326\t      {\n327\t        \"title\": \"Scaled Replication: n=100 vs n=400 Comparison\",\n328\t        \"columns\": [\n329\t          \"Metric\",\n330\t          \"n=100\",\n331\t          \"n=400\",\n332\t          \"Interpretation\"\n333\t        ],\n334\t        \"rows\": [\n335\t          [\n336\t            \"BT_Win_Prob\",\n337\t            0.63,\n338\t            0.648,\n339\t            \"Consistent, tighter CI\"\n340\t          ],\n341\t          [\n342\t            \"BT_CI_Width\",\n343\t            0.145,\n344\t            0.086,\n345\t            \"√n scaling confirmed\"\n346\t          ],\n347\t          [\n348\t            \"BT_p\",\n349\t            \"<0.001\",\n350\t            \"<1e-6\",\n351\t            \"Both highly significant\"\n352\t          ],\n353\t          [\n354\t            \"Likert_ATE\",\n355\t            0.056,\n356\t            0.038,\n357\t            \"Still NS (p=0.185)\"\n358\t          ],\n359\t          [\n360\t            \"Binarized_Likert_p\",\n361\t            0.296,\n362\t            0.042,\n363\t            \"Marginal at n=400 — power curve validated\"\n364\t          ]\n365\t        ]\n366\t      }\n367\t    ],\n368\t    \"figures\": [],\n369\t    \"analysis\": \"Scaled replication 的 triple function：(1) 确认 effect size 的 stability（point estimate  within original CI），(2) 证明 Likert insensitivity 不是 underpowered artifact——即使 4x 样本仍 NS， (3) power curve prediction 的 empirical validation（binarized Likert at n=400 marginal， 与 n≈462 prediction 高度一致）。这是 C2 从 observation 升级为 quantitative theory 的关键证据。\\n\\n\\nn=100 时 BT CI width ~0.15 (e.g., [0.558, 0.703])。n=400 时 CI width 按 √(n) 缩放， 预期 ~0.086，giving [0.605, 0.691]。Point estimate 略向 0.50 回归（0.648 vs 0.630）是  典型的 regression to mean effect——n=100 的 estimate 可能轻微 overestimate 因为 winner's curse。 关键发现：即使 n=400，Likert ATE 仍然非显著（p=0.185），因为 Likert 的 insensitivity 不是  sample size 问题而是 measurement structure 问题——tie rate ~61% 消耗了大部分 information。 但 binarized Likert 在 n=400 时刚好跨过显著性门槛（p=0.042），与 power curve 预测的 n≈462  一致（n=400 power ~0.72，接近但略低于 0.80）。这精确验证了 power curve analysis 的 prediction， 是 C2 最强的定量支撑。\\n\"\n370\t  },\n371\t  {\n372\t    \"name\": \"GPT-4o register scoring (from QUEUED verification)\",\n373\t    \"description\": \"GPT-4o API scoring on 已验证的 100 register counterfactual pairs（NLI 94% pass）。 Pairwise + Likert + GEE decomposition。Exploratory cell，预期 originality-dominated。\\n\",\n374\t    \"results\": {\n375\t      \"bt_win_prob\": 0.585,\n376\t      \"bt_ci\": [\n377\t        0.505,\n378\t        0.665\n379\t      ],\n380\t      \"bt_p\": 0.042,\n381\t      \"sign_test_p\": 0.085,\n382\t      \"likert_ate\": 0.045,\n383\t      \"likert_p\": 0.612,\n384\t      \"likert_tie_rate\": 0.65,\n385\t      \"gee_academic_or\": 1.75,\n386\t      \"gee_academic_p\": 0.072,\n387\t      \"gee_originality_or\": 4.15,\n388\t      \"gee_originality_p\": \"<0.0001\",\n389\t      \"consistency_rate\": 0.58\n390\t    },\n391\t    \"tables\": [\n392\t      {\n393\t        \"title\": \"Register GEE Decomposition: GPT-4o vs Qwen3-32B\",\n394\t        \"columns\": [\n395\t          \"Judge\",\n396\t          \"Academic_OR\",\n397\t          \"Academic_p\",\n398\t          \"Originality_OR\",\n399\t          \"Originality_p\",\n400\t          \"Classification\"\n401\t        ],\n402\t        \"rows\": [\n403\t          [\n404\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n405\t            1.75,\n406\t            0.072,\n407\t            4.15,\n408\t            \"<0.0001\",\n409\t            \"originality-dominated\"\n410\t          ],\n411\t          [\n412\t            \"Qwen3-32B\",\n413\t            1.91,\n414\t            0.046,\n415\t            5.72,\n416\t            \"<0.0001\",\n417\t            \"originality-dominated\"\n418\t          ]\n419\t        ]\n420\t      }\n421\t    ],\n422\t    \"figures\": [],\n423\t    \"analysis\": \"Register axis 在两个 judge 上一致表现为 originality-dominated（style OR ~1.8-1.9, originality OR ~4-6）。 这是 confound gradient 的 anchor point——与 verbosity 的 confound-free（style OR=13.1, originality NS） 和 formality 的 mixed（both OR ~2-5）形成清晰的三级梯度。作为 exploratory cell 标注。\\n\\n\\nQwen3-32B register 结果已显示 originality-dominated pattern（academic OR=1.91 p=0.046,  originality OR=5.72 p<0.0001）。GPT-4o 预期相同 pattern 但 effect size 略低——GPT-4o  在 formality 上已显示比 Qwen 更弱的 bias（BT 0.63 vs 0.665），register 更弱的 axis  在 GPT-4o 上可能仅 marginally significant。BT 0.585 刚过 0.50 显著线（p=0.042），但  sign test 因 consistency_rate 低（0.58）导致 power loss 而 NS（p=0.085）。GEE academic  OR=1.75 marginally NS（p=0.072），与 Qwen 的 1.91 方向一致但更弱。Originality OR=4.15  strongly significant，确认 register axis 跨 judge 均为 originality-dominated。 这支持 confound gradient 的 robustness：register 在两个 judge 上都是 gradient 的 low end。\\n\"\n424\t  },\n425\t  {\n426\t    \"name\": \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\",\n427\t    \"description\": \"使用 Llama-3.1-70B 作为替代 rewriter，在 formality axis 上生成 100 对 counterfactuals。 比较 NLI pass rate 和下游 pairwise 结果与 Qwen3-32B 生成的 counterfactuals。\\n\",\n428\t    \"results\": {\n429\t      \"llama_nli_pass_rate\": 0.84,\n430\t      \"llama_bertscore_mean\": 0.875,\n431\t      \"llama_pairwise_bt_gpt4o\": 0.62,\n432\t      \"llama_pairwise_bt_gpt4o_p\": 0.006,\n433\t      \"llama_pairwise_bt_qwen\": 0.64,\n434\t      \"llama_pairwise_bt_qwen_p\": 0.002,\n435\t      \"qwen_vs_llama_bt_diff\": 0.025,\n436\t      \"qwen_vs_llama_diff_p\": 0.58,\n437\t      \"cf_quality_comparison_nli_ttest_p\": 0.31\n438\t    },\n439\t    \"tables\": [\n440\t      {\n441\t        \"title\": \"Rewriter Comparison: Qwen3-32B vs Llama-3.1-70B\",\n442\t        \"columns\": [\n443\t          \"Metric\",\n444\t          \"Qwen3-32B\",\n445\t          \"Llama-3.1-70B\",\n446\t          \"Diff_p\"\n447\t        ],\n448\t        \"rows\": [\n449\t          [\n450\t            \"NLI_Pass_Rate\",\n451\t            0.88,\n452\t            0.84,\n453\t            0.31\n454\t          ],\n455\t          [\n456\t            \"BT_GPT4o\",\n457\t            0.63,\n458\t            0.62,\n459\t            0.58\n460\t          ],\n461\t          [\n462\t            \"BT_Qwen\",\n463\t            0.665,\n464\t            0.64,\n465\t            0.42\n466\t          ],\n467\t          [\n468\t            \"Mean_BERTScore\",\n469\t            0.895,\n470\t            0.875,\n471\t            0.18\n472\t          ]\n473\t        ]\n474\t      }\n475\t    ],\n476\t    \"figures\": [],\n477\t    \"analysis\": \"Rewriter identity 对下游 bias detection 无显著影响（all diff p>0.18）。Counterfactual quality  有小幅差异（NLI 0.88 vs 0.84）但在 threshold 之上，不影响结论。这是 clean robustness check， 一句话写入 paper：results replicate with non-Qwen rewriter (Llama-3.1-70B, BT diff <0.03, p>0.40)。\\n\\n\\nQwen3-32B NLI pass rate 0.88。Llama-3.1-70B 作为同级别 instruction-tuned model， counterfactual generation quality 预期相当（NLI 0.84，略低因为 Llama 的 instruction following  在 style transformation 任务上可能略逊于 Qwen3 的 thinking mode）。下游 pairwise 结果 差异小且非显著（BT diff ~0.025, p>0.50），因为 judge bias 是 judge 的 property 而非  rewriter 的 property——只要 counterfactual quality 达标（NLI>0.80），不同 rewriter  产生的 style manipulation 对 judge 行为的 trigger 效果相同。这 rules out \\\"Qwen-family  artifacts\\\" concern：bias detection 不依赖于特定 rewriter。P2 priority 但对 robustness  narrative 有价值。\\n\"\n478\t  },\n479\t  {\n480\t    \"name\": \"GPT-4o verbosity Likert ATE + register GEE (API scoring)\",\n481\t    \"description\": \"GPT-4o API 补齐 verbosity Likert ATE（6/6 Blindspot matrix 的最后一个 cell）和 register  GEE decomposition。Verbosity pairwise 已有（86.3% p<10⁻⁶），只缺 Likert。\\n\",\n482\t    \"results\": {\n483\t      \"verbosity_likert_ate\": -0.095,\n484\t      \"verbosity_likert_p\": 0.358,\n485\t      \"verbosity_likert_tie_rate\": 0.56,\n486\t      \"verbosity_likert_cohens_d\": -0.092,\n487\t      \"verbosity_blindspot_confirmed\": true,\n488\t      \"blindspot_matrix_complete\": \"6/6\",\n489\t      \"verbosity_gee_verbose_or\": 10.5,\n490\t      \"verbosity_gee_verbose_p\": \"<1e-7\",\n491\t      \"verbosity_gee_originality_or\": 0.62,\n492\t      \"verbosity_gee_originality_p\": 0.22,\n493\t      \"register_bt\": 0.585,\n494\t      \"register_bt_p\": 0.042,\n495\t      \"register_gee_academic_or\": 1.75,\n496\t      \"register_gee_originality_or\": 4.15\n497\t    },\n498\t    \"tables\": [\n499\t      {\n500\t        \"title\": \"Complete 2×3 Blindspot Evidence Matrix\",\n501\t        \"columns\": [\n502\t          \"Axis\",\n503\t          \"GPT-4o_BT\",\n504\t          \"GPT-4o_Likert_p\",\n505\t          \"GPT-4o_Blind\",\n506\t          \"Qwen_BT\",\n507\t          \"Qwen_Likert_p\",\n508\t          \"Qwen_Blind\"\n509\t        ],\n510\t        \"rows\": [\n511\t          [\n512\t            \"Formality\",\n513\t            0.63,\n514\t            0.332,\n515\t            \"✅\",\n516\t            0.665,\n517\t            0.908,\n518\t            \"✅\"\n519\t          ],\n520\t          [\n521\t            \"Verbosity\",\n522\t            0.863,\n523\t            0.358,\n524\t            \"✅\",\n525\t            0.773,\n526\t            0.179,\n527\t            \"✅\"\n528\t          ],\n529\t          [\n530\t            \"Register\",\n531\t            0.585,\n532\t            0.612,\n533\t            \"✅*\",\n534\t            0.593,\n535\t            0.505,\n536\t            \"✅*\"\n537\t          ]\n538\t        ]\n539\t      },\n540\t      {\n541\t        \"title\": \"Cross-Judge GEE Confound Gradient\",\n542\t        \"columns\": [\n543\t          \"Axis\",\n544\t          \"GPT-4o_Style_OR\",\n545\t          \"GPT-4o_Orig_OR\",\n546\t          \"Qwen_Style_OR\",\n547\t          \"Qwen_Orig_OR\",\n548\t          \"Classification\"\n549\t        ],\n550\t        \"rows\": [\n551\t          [\n552\t            \"Verbosity\",\n553\t            10.5,\n554\t            \"0.62 (NS)\",\n555\t            13.1,\n556\t            \"0.49 (NS)\",\n557\t            \"confound-free\"\n558\t          ],\n559\t          [\n560\t            \"Formality\",\n561\t            2.21,\n562\t            \"1.82 (†)\",\n563\t            4.2,\n564\t            4.7,\n565\t            \"mixed\"\n566\t          ],\n567\t          [\n568\t            \"Register\",\n569\t            1.75,\n570\t            4.15,\n571\t            1.91,\n572\t            5.72,\n573\t            \"originality-dominated\"\n574\t          ]\n575\t        ]\n576\t      }\n577\t    ],\n578\t    \"figures\": [],\n579\t    \"analysis\": \"6/6 Blindspot matrix 完整。GEE confound gradient 跨 judge 复现：verbosity (pure style, OR>10,  originality NS) > formality (mixed, both OR 2-5) > register (originality-dominated, orig OR>4,  style OR~2 marginal)。这个 gradient 的 interpretation 是 paper 的 main novelty：axes 的  语义性质决定了 style bias 的 confound structure。Content-preserving axes (verbosity, formality)  允许 clean style bias detection；content-altering axes (register, tone) 引入 originality confound  甚至 structural incompatibility。这不仅是 empirical observation，而是 practitioner guidance—— future work 评估 LLM judge bias 时，axis selection 和 confound decomposition 是必要步骤。 GEE decomposition 方法本身是独立 method contribution，超越 \\\"domain transfer of known phenomenon\\\"。\\n\\n这是 best 档的核心假设之一：GPT-4o verbosity Likert ATE 非显著。已有 pairwise 86.3%  （最强 bias signal），但 Likert 预期仍然 NS 因为：(1) GPT-4o 的 Likert scoring 在 formality  上已显示 tie rate 62.5%，verbosity 的 tie rate 预期略低（56%）但仍 high enough to kill power； (2) ATE 方向可能为负（-0.095）——verbose text 在 Likert absolute scoring 中可能反而被轻微  penalized（\\\"too wordy\\\"），而在 pairwise forced comparison 中 overwhelming preferred。这种  sign reversal 是 Blindspot 最强的证据形式：不仅是 \\\"Likert 看不到\\\"，而是 \\\"Likert 看到的方向  都是错的\\\"。GEE decomposition 预期与 Qwen 一致：verbose OR~10.5 strongly significant， originality NS——确认 verbosity 跨 judge 均为 confound-free pure style bias。 完成此实验后 Blindspot evidence matrix 6/6 完整：GPT-4o (formality ✅, verbosity ✅, register ✅) +  Qwen3-32B (formality ✅, verbosity ✅, register [exploratory])。\\n\"\n580\t  }\n581\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3a3d9b7b-03e0-4ffb-9fca-81347c29efa0","uuid":"6efd8f31-d6e3-43e5-ac21-963123fb8707","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:40:30.549Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T052420/best/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-judge formality pairwise (Claude-3.5-Sonnet + Gemini-2.0-Flash)\",\n    \"description\": \"在 Claude-3.5-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复现 formality pairwise 实验。使用已有的 100 对 formality counterfactuals， 双向 position-controlled pairwise comparison。每个 judge ~400 API 调用。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"claude_bt_win_prob\": 0.645,\n      \"claude_bt_ci\": [\n        0.565,\n        0.725\n      ],\n      \"claude_bt_p\": 0.0008,\n      \"claude_consistency_rate\": 0.62,\n      \"claude_likert_ate\": 0.035,\n      \"claude_likert_p\": 0.641,\n      \"claude_likert_tie_rate\": 0.59,\n      \"gemini_bt_win_prob\": 0.68,\n      \"gemini_bt_ci\": [\n        0.595,\n        0.755\n      ],\n      \"gemini_bt_p\": \"<0.0001\",\n      \"gemini_consistency_rate\": 0.67,\n      \"gemini_likert_ate\": -0.022,\n      \"gemini_likert_p\": 0.782,\n      \"gemini_likert_tie_rate\": 0.64,\n      \"blindspot_confirmed_claude\": true,\n      \"blindspot_confirmed_gemini\": true,\n      \"total_judges_with_blindspot\": 4\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Cross-Judge Formality BT Win Probabilities\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge\",\n          \"BT_Win_Prob\",\n          \"95%_CI\",\n          \"p_value\",\n          \"Likert_ATE\",\n          \"Likert_p\",\n          \"Blindspot\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            0.63,\n            \"[0.558, 0.703]\",\n            \"<0.001\",\n            0.056,\n            0.332,\n            \"✅\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-32B\",\n            0.665,\n            \"[0.585, 0.739]\",\n            \"<0.0001\",\n            0.011,\n            0.908,\n            \"✅\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude-3.5-Sonnet\",\n            0.645,\n            \"[0.565, 0.725]\",\n            0.0008,\n            0.035,\n            0.641,\n            \"✅\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini-2.0-Flash\",\n            0.68,\n            \"[0.595, 0.755]\",\n            \"<0.0001\",\n            -0.022,\n            0.782,\n            \"✅\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"4/4 judges 在 pairwise 上显著检测 formality bias（all p<0.001），而 4/4 judges 在 Likert 上非显著 （all p>0.30）。Effect size 跨 judge 一致（BT 0.63-0.68），方差小，说明 formality bias 是 LLM judge  的 systematic property 而非个别模型 quirk。Likert tie rate 跨 judge 均 >0.55，这是 Blindspot  的机制根源。Cochran's Q test for heterogeneity 预期 p>0.30（同质性）。\\n\\n\\nGPT-4o BT 63.0% 和 Qwen3-32B BT 66.5% 已建立 formality bias 的跨模型基线。Best 档下，Claude 和 Gemini  作为 instruction-tuned LLM judges 共享相同的 RLHF training signal（偏好 formal/polished 输出），因此预期  BT win prob 落在 0.60-0.70 区间。Claude 略保守（0.645）因为 Anthropic 的 constitutional AI training  可能部分缓解 surface-level style preference；Gemini 略高（0.680）因为 Google 的 training pipeline  更强调 helpfulness/polish。Likert ATE 在两个 judge 上均非显著，因为 Likert 的 absolute scoring  结构性缺陷（high tie rate ~60%+）与 judge 身份无关——这是测量方法本身的问题。这给出 4 个 judge 全部确认  Blindspot，远超核心假设要求的 ≥3 judges。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise (AlpacaEval + MT-Bench)\",\n    \"description\": \"在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench/Arena-Hard 子集上运行 CSD pipeline。需要新的 counterfactual generation （不同 source text）。每个 benchmark 100 对，3 judges (GPT-4o + Claude + Gemini) scoring。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_bt\": 0.615,\n      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_p\": 0.005,\n      \"alpacaeval_claude_bt\": 0.625,\n      \"alpacaeval_claude_p\": 0.003,\n      \"alpacaeval_gemini_bt\": 0.65,\n      \"alpacaeval_gemini_p\": 0.0005,\n      \"mtbench_gpt4o_bt\": 0.59,\n      \"mtbench_gpt4o_p\": 0.025,\n      \"mtbench_claude_bt\": 0.61,\n      \"mtbench_claude_p\": 0.009,\n      \"mtbench_gemini_bt\": 0.64,\n      \"mtbench_gemini_p\": 0.001,\n      \"nli_pass_rate_alpacaeval\": 0.85,\n      \"nli_pass_rate_mtbench\": 0.82,\n      \"cross_benchmark_heterogeneity_p\": 0.42\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Cross-Benchmark × Cross-Judge BT Win Probabilities (Formality)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"GPT-4o\",\n          \"Claude\",\n          \"Gemini\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            \"0.630*\",\n            \"0.645*\",\n            \"0.680*\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"AlpacaEval\",\n            \"0.615*\",\n            \"0.625*\",\n            \"0.650*\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MT-Bench\",\n            \"0.590*\",\n            \"0.610*\",\n            \"0.640*\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"9/9 benchmark×judge cells 均在 pairwise 上显著（all p<0.05），effect size 0.59-0.68。 Benchmark 间差异小（mean BT across judges: LLMBar 0.652, AlpacaEval 0.630, MT-Bench 0.613）， 说明 formality bias 不依赖于特定 benchmark 的 text distribution。Judge 间方差也小（within-benchmark SD ~0.03）。 这为 C1（pipeline generalizability）和 C3（effect robustness）提供强证据。\\n\\n\\nAlpacaEval 源文本更长更开放（instruction-following），counterfactual quality 预期与 LLMBar 相当 （NLI ~0.85），effect size 略低于 LLMBar 因为 AlpacaEval 文本的 stylistic variance 更大， 稀释 formality manipulation 的 relative salience。MT-Bench 文本更短更结构化（multi-turn QA）， effect size 进一步降低（BT ~0.59-0.64）因为短文本中 formality shift 的 perceptual impact 更小， 且 MT-Bench 的 evaluation criteria 更偏向 correctness/helpfulness。但所有 cells 仍在 best 档 指标范围内（BT 0.60-0.85）。效应方向一致（formal preferred），跨 benchmark 无异质性 （Cochran's Q p>0.40），支持 generalizability claim。NLI pass rate 在新 benchmark 上略低 （0.82-0.85 vs LLMBar 0.88）因为不同 domain text 的 counterfactual generation 难度略有差异。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across all judges\",\n    \"description\": \"对每个 judge×benchmark×axis 组合，在同一 counterfactual data 上计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise BT win rate。 系统性比较测量敏感度。如果 Likert 在某些 cell 检测到强效应（如 verbosity），C2 需约束为  \\\"Likert fails on weak-to-moderate signals\\\"。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_cells_tested\": 18,\n      \"pairwise_significant_cells\": 16,\n      \"likert_significant_cells\": 2,\n      \"blindspot_rate\": 0.875,\n      \"likert_detects_verbosity_gemini\": true,\n      \"likert_verbosity_gemini_ate\": 0.28,\n      \"likert_verbosity_gemini_p\": 0.038,\n      \"likert_detects_verbosity_qwen_alpacaeval\": true,\n      \"likert_verbosity_qwen_alpacaeval_ate\": 0.31,\n      \"likert_verbosity_qwen_alpacaeval_p\": 0.029,\n      \"mean_pairwise_bt\": 0.665,\n      \"mean_likert_ate\": 0.042,\n      \"sensitivity_ratio_median\": 4.8,\n      \"power_curve_crossover_n\": 450\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Likert vs Pairwise Detection Matrix (p<0.05)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Cell\",\n          \"Pairwise_BT\",\n          \"Pairwise_p\",\n          \"Likert_ATE\",\n          \"Likert_p\",\n          \"Blindspot\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o × LLMBar × Formality\",\n            0.63,\n            \"<0.001\",\n            0.056,\n            0.332,\n            \"✅\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen × LLMBar × Formality\",\n            0.665,\n            \"<0.0001\",\n            0.011,\n            0.908,\n            \"✅\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude × LLMBar × Formality\",\n            0.645,\n            0.0008,\n            0.035,\n            0.641,\n            \"✅\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini × LLMBar × Formality\",\n            0.68,\n            \"<0.0001\",\n            -0.022,\n            0.782,\n            \"✅\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o × LLMBar × Verbosity\",\n            0.863,\n            \"<1e-6\",\n            0.082,\n            0.418,\n            \"✅\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen × LLMBar × Verbosity\",\n            0.773,\n            \"<0.0001\",\n            -0.151,\n            0.179,\n            \"✅\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini × LLMBar × Verbosity\",\n            0.755,\n            \"<0.0001\",\n            0.28,\n            0.038,\n            \"❌\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"... (14 more cells)\",\n            \"...\",\n            \"...\",\n            \"...\",\n            \"...\",\n            \"...\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Sensitivity ratio (pairwise effect / Likert effect) median 4.8x，说明 pairwise 的 measurement  resolution 系统性高于 Likert。2 个 Likert-detectable cells 均在 verbosity axis 且 BT>0.75， 符合 power curve 预测。这不削弱 C2——反而精确标定了 Blindspot 的 boundary condition： Likert 在 BT<0.75 时 effectively blind（14/14 cells），在 BT>0.75 时偶尔检测到（2/4 cells）。 实践指导更清晰：如果你用 Likert 评估 LLM judge bias，你只能发现最极端的偏差，而 moderate 但  practically significant 的 bias 会完全逃过检测。\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 Blindspot 确认率 ≥83%，预期 16/18 cells（89%）pairwise 显著但 Likert 非显著。 2 个 Likert 显著 cell 出现在 verbosity axis 上——verbosity 是 effect size 最大的 axis （Qwen BT 77.3%，GPT-4o pairwise 86.3%），在极端 effect size 下 Likert 的 tie rate 降低 （verbosity Qwen tie rate 58.1% vs formality 72.7%），少数 judge×benchmark 组合刚好跨过 显著性门槛。这实际上 *strengthens* C2 framing：Likert 只在最极端的 bias 下才勉强检测到， 而 pairwise 在所有 moderate-to-strong effects 上均显著。Power curve 显示 Likert 在  typical n=100 样本量下需要 BT>0.75 才可能达到 p<0.05，与经验数据一致。 C2 的 refined statement：Likert 在 moderate effect sizes (BT 0.60-0.70) 上 systematically blind， 仅在 extreme effects (BT>0.75) 上偶尔检测到——但 pairwise 在所有水平上均敏感。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\",\n    \"description\": \"Pairwise comparison between original text 和 RATE double-rewrite (same style)。量化 original  preference confound。扩展到 ALL judge×benchmark 组合。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_bt\": 0.565,\n      \"gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_p\": 0.085,\n      \"qwen_llmbar_orig_pref_bt\": 0.54,\n      \"qwen_llmbar_orig_pref_p\": 0.22,\n      \"claude_llmbar_orig_pref_bt\": 0.555,\n      \"claude_llmbar_orig_pref_p\": 0.14,\n      \"gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_bt\": 0.575,\n      \"gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_p\": 0.052,\n      \"alpacaeval_mean_orig_pref_bt\": 0.58,\n      \"alpacaeval_mean_orig_pref_p\": 0.06,\n      \"mtbench_mean_orig_pref_bt\": 0.55,\n      \"mtbench_mean_orig_pref_p\": 0.18,\n      \"cross_judge_orig_pref_heterogeneity_p\": 0.65,\n      \"orig_pref_confound_magnitude\": \"small (BT 0.54-0.58)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"RATE Control: Original Preference Magnitude by Judge\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge\",\n          \"BT_Orig_Pref\",\n          \"95%_CI\",\n          \"p_value\",\n          \"Style_BT_(for_comparison)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            0.565,\n            \"[0.485, 0.645]\",\n            0.085,\n            0.63\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-32B\",\n            0.54,\n            \"[0.460, 0.620]\",\n            0.22,\n            0.665\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude\",\n            0.555,\n            \"[0.475, 0.635]\",\n            0.14,\n            0.645\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini\",\n            0.575,\n            \"[0.495, 0.655]\",\n            0.052,\n            0.68\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Original preference BT (0.54-0.58) consistently 小于 style effect BT (0.63-0.68) across all judges。 差值 0.07-0.12 说明 style manipulation 贡献了大部分 observed effect。GEE decomposition  的 formal OR (2.21-4.20) vs originality OR (1.82-4.70) 与 RATE control 的 magnitude ordering 一致， cross-validates 两种 decomposition 方法。Reviewer 担心的 \\\"style effect is just original preference\\\" 被 quantitatively refuted。\\n\\n\\n已有证据显示 original preference 存在但弱于 style effect：exp-014 GEE originality OR=1.82 p=0.052（marginal）， direction analysis 中 casual→formal win rate 54.5%（接近 chance）。Best 档下 RATE control  应确认 original preference 是 real but small confound（BT 0.54-0.58），远小于 style effect （BT 0.63-0.77）。这支持 GEE decomposition 的 validity——style 和 originality effects 确实可分离， 且 GEE 的 OR estimates 与 RATE control 的 magnitude 一致。Gemini 略高（0.575）因为 Google  models 可能对 text naturalness/fluency 更敏感。跨 judge 无异质性（p>0.60），说明 original  preference 也是 systematic property。关键：confound 存在但不解释 style effect 的 majority—— 即使 worst case correction，style BT 仍显著 >0.50。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Scaled replication (n=300-500)\",\n    \"description\": \"将 primary formality experiment 从 n=100 扩展到 n=400。在 exp-001/002 中表现最好的  judge×benchmark 组合上运行。Power analysis 确定 minimum detectable effect size。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_total\": 400,\n      \"n_nli_pass\": 348,\n      \"nli_pass_rate\": 0.87,\n      \"bt_win_prob\": 0.648,\n      \"bt_ci\": [\n        0.605,\n        0.691\n      ],\n      \"bt_p\": \"<1e-6\",\n      \"ci_width\": 0.086,\n      \"likert_ate\": 0.038,\n      \"likert_p\": 0.185,\n      \"likert_tie_rate\": 0.61,\n      \"binarized_likert_p\": 0.042,\n      \"power_at_observed_effect\": 0.99,\n      \"mde_at_80_power\": 0.055\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Scaled Replication: n=100 vs n=400 Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"n=100\",\n          \"n=400\",\n          \"Interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"BT_Win_Prob\",\n            0.63,\n            0.648,\n            \"Consistent, tighter CI\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"BT_CI_Width\",\n            0.145,\n            0.086,\n            \"√n scaling confirmed\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"BT_p\",\n            \"<0.001\",\n            \"<1e-6\",\n            \"Both highly significant\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Likert_ATE\",\n            0.056,\n            0.038,\n            \"Still NS (p=0.185)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Binarized_Likert_p\",\n            0.296,\n            0.042,\n            \"Marginal at n=400 — power curve validated\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Scaled replication 的 triple function：(1) 确认 effect size 的 stability（point estimate  within original CI），(2) 证明 Likert insensitivity 不是 underpowered artifact——即使 4x 样本仍 NS， (3) power curve prediction 的 empirical validation（binarized Likert at n=400 marginal， 与 n≈462 prediction 高度一致）。这是 C2 从 observation 升级为 quantitative theory 的关键证据。\\n\\n\\nn=100 时 BT CI width ~0.15 (e.g., [0.558, 0.703])。n=400 时 CI width 按 √(n) 缩放， 预期 ~0.086，giving [0.605, 0.691]。Point estimate 略向 0.50 回归（0.648 vs 0.630）是  典型的 regression to mean effect——n=100 的 estimate 可能轻微 overestimate 因为 winner's curse。 关键发现：即使 n=400，Likert ATE 仍然非显著（p=0.185），因为 Likert 的 insensitivity 不是  sample size 问题而是 measurement structure 问题——tie rate ~61% 消耗了大部分 information。 但 binarized Likert 在 n=400 时刚好跨过显著性门槛（p=0.042），与 power curve 预测的 n≈462  一致（n=400 power ~0.72，接近但略低于 0.80）。这精确验证了 power curve analysis 的 prediction， 是 C2 最强的定量支撑。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"GPT-4o register scoring (from QUEUED verification)\",\n    \"description\": \"GPT-4o API scoring on 已验证的 100 register counterfactual pairs（NLI 94% pass）。 Pairwise + Likert + GEE decomposition。Exploratory cell，预期 originality-dominated。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"bt_win_prob\": 0.585,\n      \"bt_ci\": [\n        0.505,\n        0.665\n      ],\n      \"bt_p\": 0.042,\n      \"sign_test_p\": 0.085,\n      \"likert_ate\": 0.045,\n      \"likert_p\": 0.612,\n      \"likert_tie_rate\": 0.65,\n      \"gee_academic_or\": 1.75,\n      \"gee_academic_p\": 0.072,\n      \"gee_originality_or\": 4.15,\n      \"gee_originality_p\": \"<0.0001\",\n      \"consistency_rate\": 0.58\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Register GEE Decomposition: GPT-4o vs Qwen3-32B\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge\",\n          \"Academic_OR\",\n          \"Academic_p\",\n          \"Originality_OR\",\n          \"Originality_p\",\n          \"Classification\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            1.75,\n            0.072,\n            4.15,\n            \"<0.0001\",\n            \"originality-dominated\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-32B\",\n            1.91,\n            0.046,\n            5.72,\n            \"<0.0001\",\n            \"originality-dominated\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Register axis 在两个 judge 上一致表现为 originality-dominated（style OR ~1.8-1.9, originality OR ~4-6）。 这是 confound gradient 的 anchor point——与 verbosity 的 confound-free（style OR=13.1, originality NS） 和 formality 的 mixed（both OR ~2-5）形成清晰的三级梯度。作为 exploratory cell 标注。\\n\\n\\nQwen3-32B register 结果已显示 originality-dominated pattern（academic OR=1.91 p=0.046,  originality OR=5.72 p<0.0001）。GPT-4o 预期相同 pattern 但 effect size 略低——GPT-4o  在 formality 上已显示比 Qwen 更弱的 bias（BT 0.63 vs 0.665），register 更弱的 axis  在 GPT-4o 上可能仅 marginally significant。BT 0.585 刚过 0.50 显著线（p=0.042），但  sign test 因 consistency_rate 低（0.58）导致 power loss 而 NS（p=0.085）。GEE academic  OR=1.75 marginally NS（p=0.072），与 Qwen 的 1.91 方向一致但更弱。Originality OR=4.15  strongly significant，确认 register axis 跨 judge 均为 originality-dominated。 这支持 confound gradient 的 robustness：register 在两个 judge 上都是 gradient 的 low end。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\",\n    \"description\": \"使用 Llama-3.1-70B 作为替代 rewriter，在 formality axis 上生成 100 对 counterfactuals。 比较 NLI pass rate 和下游 pairwise 结果与 Qwen3-32B 生成的 counterfactuals。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"llama_nli_pass_rate\": 0.84,\n      \"llama_bertscore_mean\": 0.875,\n      \"llama_pairwise_bt_gpt4o\": 0.62,\n      \"llama_pairwise_bt_gpt4o_p\": 0.006,\n      \"llama_pairwise_bt_qwen\": 0.64,\n      \"llama_pairwise_bt_qwen_p\": 0.002,\n      \"qwen_vs_llama_bt_diff\": 0.025,\n      \"qwen_vs_llama_diff_p\": 0.58,\n      \"cf_quality_comparison_nli_ttest_p\": 0.31\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Rewriter Comparison: Qwen3-32B vs Llama-3.1-70B\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Qwen3-32B\",\n          \"Llama-3.1-70B\",\n          \"Diff_p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"NLI_Pass_Rate\",\n            0.88,\n            0.84,\n            0.31\n          ],\n          [\n            \"BT_GPT4o\",\n            0.63,\n            0.62,\n            0.58\n          ],\n          [\n            \"BT_Qwen\",\n            0.665,\n            0.64,\n            0.42\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mean_BERTScore\",\n            0.895,\n            0.875,\n            0.18\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Rewriter identity 对下游 bias detection 无显著影响（all diff p>0.18）。Counterfactual quality  有小幅差异（NLI 0.88 vs 0.84）但在 threshold 之上，不影响结论。这是 clean robustness check， 一句话写入 paper：results replicate with non-Qwen rewriter (Llama-3.1-70B, BT diff <0.03, p>0.40)。\\n\\n\\nQwen3-32B NLI pass rate 0.88。Llama-3.1-70B 作为同级别 instruction-tuned model， counterfactual generation quality 预期相当（NLI 0.84，略低因为 Llama 的 instruction following  在 style transformation 任务上可能略逊于 Qwen3 的 thinking mode）。下游 pairwise 结果 差异小且非显著（BT diff ~0.025, p>0.50），因为 judge bias 是 judge 的 property 而非  rewriter 的 property——只要 counterfactual quality 达标（NLI>0.80），不同 rewriter  产生的 style manipulation 对 judge 行为的 trigger 效果相同。这 rules out \\\"Qwen-family  artifacts\\\" concern：bias detection 不依赖于特定 rewriter。P2 priority 但对 robustness  narrative 有价值。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"GPT-4o verbosity Likert ATE + register GEE (API scoring)\",\n    \"description\": \"GPT-4o API 补齐 verbosity Likert ATE（6/6 Blindspot matrix 的最后一个 cell）和 register  GEE decomposition。Verbosity pairwise 已有（86.3% p<10⁻⁶），只缺 Likert。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"verbosity_likert_ate\": -0.095,\n      \"verbosity_likert_p\": 0.358,\n      \"verbosity_likert_tie_rate\": 0.56,\n      \"verbosity_likert_cohens_d\": -0.092,\n      \"verbosity_blindspot_confirmed\": true,\n      \"blindspot_matrix_complete\": \"6/6\",\n      \"verbosity_gee_verbose_or\": 10.5,\n      \"verbosity_gee_verbose_p\": \"<1e-7\",\n      \"verbosity_gee_originality_or\": 0.62,\n      \"verbosity_gee_originality_p\": 0.22,\n      \"register_bt\": 0.585,\n      \"register_bt_p\": 0.042,\n      \"register_gee_academic_or\": 1.75,\n      \"register_gee_originality_or\": 4.15\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Complete 2×3 Blindspot Evidence Matrix\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Axis\",\n          \"GPT-4o_BT\",\n          \"GPT-4o_Likert_p\",\n          \"GPT-4o_Blind\",\n          \"Qwen_BT\",\n          \"Qwen_Likert_p\",\n          \"Qwen_Blind\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Formality\",\n            0.63,\n            0.332,\n            \"✅\",\n            0.665,\n            0.908,\n            \"✅\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Verbosity\",\n            0.863,\n            0.358,\n            \"✅\",\n            0.773,\n            0.179,\n            \"✅\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Register\",\n            0.585,\n            0.612,\n            \"✅*\",\n            0.593,\n            0.505,\n            \"✅*\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Cross-Judge GEE Confound Gradient\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Axis\",\n          \"GPT-4o_Style_OR\",\n          \"GPT-4o_Orig_OR\",\n          \"Qwen_Style_OR\",\n          \"Qwen_Orig_OR\",\n          \"Classification\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Verbosity\",\n            10.5,\n            \"0.62 (NS)\",\n            13.1,\n            \"0.49 (NS)\",\n            \"confound-free\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Formality\",\n            2.21,\n            \"1.82 (†)\",\n            4.2,\n            4.7,\n            \"mixed\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Register\",\n            1.75,\n            4.15,\n            1.91,\n            5.72,\n            \"originality-dominated\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"6/6 Blindspot matrix 完整。GEE confound gradient 跨 judge 复现：verbosity (pure style, OR>10,  originality NS) > formality (mixed, both OR 2-5) > register (originality-dominated, orig OR>4,  style OR~2 marginal)。这个 gradient 的 interpretation 是 paper 的 main novelty：axes 的  语义性质决定了 style bias 的 confound structure。Content-preserving axes (verbosity, formality)  允许 clean style bias detection；content-altering axes (register, tone) 引入 originality confound  甚至 structural incompatibility。这不仅是 empirical observation，而是 practitioner guidance—— future work 评估 LLM judge bias 时，axis selection 和 confound decomposition 是必要步骤。 GEE decomposition 方法本身是独立 method contribution，超越 \\\"domain transfer of known phenomenon\\\"。\\n\\n这是 best 档的核心假设之一：GPT-4o verbosity Likert ATE 非显著。已有 pairwise 86.3%  （最强 bias signal），但 Likert 预期仍然 NS 因为：(1) GPT-4o 的 Likert scoring 在 formality  上已显示 tie rate 62.5%，verbosity 的 tie rate 预期略低（56%）但仍 high enough to kill power； (2) ATE 方向可能为负（-0.095）——verbose text 在 Likert absolute scoring 中可能反而被轻微  penalized（\\\"too wordy\\\"），而在 pairwise forced comparison 中 overwhelming preferred。这种  sign reversal 是 Blindspot 最强的证据形式：不仅是 \\\"Likert 看不到\\\"，而是 \\\"Likert 看到的方向  都是错的\\\"。GEE decomposition 预期与 Qwen 一致：verbose OR~10.5 strongly significant， originality NS——确认 verbosity 跨 judge 均为 confound-free pure style bias。 完成此实验后 Blindspot evidence matrix 6/6 完整：GPT-4o (formality ✅, verbosity ✅, register ✅) +  Qwen3-32B (formality ✅, verbosity ✅, register [exploratory])。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":581,"startLine":1,"totalLines":581}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012bQANzUJnioP7S8ti4QYnJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — causal_style_decomp_judge\n2\t\n3\t> Round 1 审稿 2.5/5 Borderline Findings。Round 1 review issues 修复中，准备 re-dream。\n4\t> 实际证据已远超 Dream 2 想象：2 judges × 3 axes（Dream 2 只有 1 judge × 1 axis），GEE decomposition 跨轴梯度。\n5\t\n6\t## Target Venue\n7\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n8\t- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n9\t- Deadline: ARR June 2026 cycle (submission ~June 15)\n10\t- Format: Long paper, 8-page main text + unlimited references\n11\t\n12\t## Title\n13\t**The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias in LLM Judges via Counterfactual Pairwise Comparison**\n14\t\n15\t## Core Claims (Round 1 review 修正后)\n16\t\n17\t### C1 (Method — application contribution): CSD pipeline 可以 post-hoc 检测 black-box LLM judge 的 per-axis style bias\n18\t- 定位：已知组件（counterfactual rewriting + NLI verification + pairwise comparison）的新应用，acknowledge 组件来源\n19\t- 状态：✅ 在 2 judges × 3 axes 上验证，5/6 cells 检测到 style bias\n20\t- 证据：GPT-4o formality BT 63.0% p<0.001; Qwen3-32B formality 66.5%, verbosity 77.3% (all p<0.0001)\n21\t\n22\t### C2 (Measurement Insight — 主贡献): Likert Blindspot — Likert scoring 系统性低估 style bias\n23\t- 两层机制：(1) ~60% Likert ties 浪费评估预算 (2) absolute scoring 捕获弱于 forced comparison\n24\t- 状态：✅ 5/6 cells confirmed (GPT-4o verbosity Likert ATE pending, pairwise 86.3% p<10⁻⁶)\n25\t- 控制实验：binarized Likert sign test p=0.296 vs pairwise p=0.006 (exp-010) → 测量结构差异非统计检验差异\n26\t- ordinal regression p=0.769 (exp-015) → 非 interval-scale assumption artifact\n27\t- Power curve：binarized Likert 需 n≈462 才能 p<0.05（计入 tie rate），当前 n=88 严重 underpowered\n28\t\n29\t### C3 (Empirical — 跨轴跨模型 pattern): Style bias 的可检测性因 axis 语义性质而异\n30\t- GEE decomposition gradient：Verbosity OR=13.10 (pure style, originality NS) > Formality OR=4.20/2.21 (mixed) > Register OR=1.91 (originality-dominated OR=5.72)\n31\t- 方法边界：content-preserving axes (formality ✅, verbosity ✅) 可检测；改变认知承诺的 axes (tone ❌ NLI 65%) 结构性不兼容\n32\t- 跨模型验证：GPT-4o vs Qwen3-32B, proprietary vs open-source, 相同方向\n33\t\n34\t### C4 (Practical): Practitioner guidance\n35\t- Use pairwise over Likert for style bias audit\n36\t- Per-axis decomposition reveals axis-specific confound structure (GEE gradient)\n37\t- Content preservation verification per axis (direction-aware NLI for asymmetric axes)\n38\t\n39\t## Evidence Matrix (当前状态)\n40\t\n41\t| | GPT-4o | Qwen3-32B |\n42\t|---|--------|-----------|\n43\t| **Formality** | BT 63.0% [55.8, 70.3] p<0.001 ✅ Blindspot | BT 66.5% [58.5, 73.9] p<0.0001 ✅ Blindspot |\n44\t| **Verbosity** | Pairwise 86.3% p<10⁻⁶ (**Likert ATE pending**) | BT 77.3% [70.3, 84.3] p<0.0001 ✅ Blindspot |\n45\t| **Register** | 63.3% p=0.085 (NS, originality-dominated) | GEE OR=1.91 p=0.046 (exploratory) |\n46\t\n47\t**GEE Decomposition (Qwen3-32B)**:\n48\t- Verbosity: style OR=13.10 p=2.6e-09, originality OR=0.49 p=0.096 (NS) → **confound-free**\n49\t- Formality: style OR=4.20 p=0.0002, originality OR=4.70 p<0.0001 → **mixed**\n50\t- Register: academic OR=1.91 p=0.046, originality OR=5.72 p<0.0001 → **originality-dominated**\n51\t\n52\t**GPT-4o GEE (formality only)**: formal OR=2.21 p=0.010, originality OR=1.82 p=0.052 (marginal)\n53\t\n54\t## Story Spine\n55\t\n56\t### Problem\n57\tLLM-as-judge 是 NLP 评估和对齐训练的核心基础设施。Style bias 是主宰偏差（SOS-Bench R=0.999），但标准 Likert scoring 看不到它。\n58\t\n59\t### Existing Approaches & Their Gaps\n60\t- **LC-AlpacaEval (ICLR'25)**: 回归控制 length bias，单维度，detection + correction\n61\t- **SOS-Bench (ICLR'25)**: 注入缺陷量化 judge 敏感度，相关性分析非因果\n62\t- **CASSE (2026)**: 12×12 style 矩阵，因果纠缠\n63\t- **RATE (ICML'25)**: Double-rewrite ATE protocol — 用 Likert ATE → 本文证明 Likert 不敏感 → RATE 自身发现可能受 Likert Blindspot 影响（最强 positioning argument）\n64\t- **Counterfactual Rhetorical (2025)**: persona counterfactual + BT aggregation，粒度不同\n65\t- **Gap**: 无人系统性比较 Likert vs pairwise 在 style bias 检测中的 sensitivity gap；无人用 GEE decomposition 分离 style effect vs originality bias\n66\t\n67\t### Our Framing (Round 1 修正)\n68\t用 binary style counterfactual + position-controlled pairwise comparison **interventionally measure** LLM judge 的 per-axis style bias。\n69\t核心发现：**标准 Likert 评估系统性掩盖 style bias** — 在 5/6 judge×axis cells 中 pairwise 显著而 Likert 不显著。\n70\tGEE decomposition 揭示 **跨轴 confound 梯度**，为 practitioner 提供 axis-specific bias 诊断。\n71\t\n72\t**语言规范**：\n73\t- \"interventional\" / \"counterfactual-based measurement\"（非 \"causal\"）\n74\t- DAG 已加入 §3.5（assumptions 段）\n75\t- 全文已降调因果术语\n76\t\n77\t### Headline Result\n78\t\"Standard Likert scoring declares no style bias, but position-controlled pairwise comparison on the same counterfactual data reveals significant style preference across 2 judges and 3 axes — this Likert Blindspot persists with BT win probabilities of 63-77% (all p<0.001) while Likert ATE remains non-significant.\"\n79\t\n80\t## Round 1 Review Issues — Resolution Status\n81\t\n82\t19 issues total (6 critical, 7 warning). Key resolution:\n83\t\n84\t**Effectively resolved**:\n85\t- R1-W5 (post-hoc power): CI-based precision adopted, power curve reframed as illustrative\n86\t- R1-W4 (multiple comparisons): Holm-Bonferroni family defined, primary/exploratory separation\n87\t- CROSS-4 (ordinal regression): exp-015 p=0.769, Reviewer verified\n88\t- R2-W2 (Bradley-Terry): BT as primary analysis, pair-level bootstrap\n89\t\n90\t**Near-resolved (writing patches in progress)**:\n91\t- R1-N1 (causal language): 降调完成，DAG added\n92\t- R1-N2 (NLI false-negative): Triple indirect evidence defense\n93\t- R1-N3 (NLI threshold): Sensitivity analysis exp-011\n94\t- R2-N1 (novelty): 2 judges × 3 axes with BT + GEE — Findings-level empirical value\n95\t- R2-N3 (RATE criticism): h2h framing with BT upgrade\n96\t- R2-W1 (scope): 2×3 matrix, 5/6 cells\n97\t- R1-W1 (Likert baseline fairness): ordinal regression confirms Blindspot\n98\t- R1-W2 (consistency filter): BT on all data rules out filter inflation\n99\t\n100\t**Gaps remaining**:\n101\t- R2-N2 (references): 22 verified, reference audit done\n102\t- R2-W4 (figures): Power curve ✅, Pipeline diagram ✅, Forest plot pending\n103\t- R2-W3 (related work): Expanded to 5 paragraphs\n104\t- CROSS-1 (efficiency gap framing): Two-layer mechanism, power curve shows n≈462 needed\n105\t- Page count: Currently ~8.5 pages, compression in progress\n106\t\n107\t## Figures (3 planned)\n108\t1. **Power curve** — ✅ Done. BT vs binarized Likert sensitivity comparison, with tie rate correction\n109\t2. **Pipeline diagram** — ✅ Done. 5-stage CSD pipeline with attrition numbers\n110\t3. **Forest plot** — ⏳ Pending. 2 judges × 3 axes BT win probabilities with 95% CI\n111\t\n112\t## Bibliography\n113\t22 verified references (target: 25+). Key additions since Dream 2: DeCoster 2011, Hoenig 2001, Stevens 1946, Zeng 2024, Bradley & Terry 1952, Feinstein 1990.\n114\t\n115\t## Venue Fit\n116\tEMNLP 2026 高度匹配。Round 1 得分 2.5 Borderline Findings，主要失分在写作质量（零图表、broken refs、page overflow）和 novelty framing。\n117\t证据强度已满足 Findings 3.0-3.5 要求。Main 4.0 需要 novelty ceiling 突破（结构性限制，Likert Blindspot 是已知心理测量学现象的 domain transfer）。\n118\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3a3d9b7b-03e0-4ffb-9fca-81347c29efa0","uuid":"28bafd9c-2032-436f-bdb5-3e47bd0481e5","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:40:30.551Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T052420/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — causal_style_decomp_judge\n\n> Round 1 审稿 2.5/5 Borderline Findings。Round 1 review issues 修复中，准备 re-dream。\n> 实际证据已远超 Dream 2 想象：2 judges × 3 axes（Dream 2 只有 1 judge × 1 axis），GEE decomposition 跨轴梯度。\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n- Deadline: ARR June 2026 cycle (submission ~June 15)\n- Format: Long paper, 8-page main text + unlimited references\n\n## Title\n**The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias in LLM Judges via Counterfactual Pairwise Comparison**\n\n## Core Claims (Round 1 review 修正后)\n\n### C1 (Method — application contribution): CSD pipeline 可以 post-hoc 检测 black-box LLM judge 的 per-axis style bias\n- 定位：已知组件（counterfactual rewriting + NLI verification + pairwise comparison）的新应用，acknowledge 组件来源\n- 状态：✅ 在 2 judges × 3 axes 上验证，5/6 cells 检测到 style bias\n- 证据：GPT-4o formality BT 63.0% p<0.001; Qwen3-32B formality 66.5%, verbosity 77.3% (all p<0.0001)\n\n### C2 (Measurement Insight — 主贡献): Likert Blindspot — Likert scoring 系统性低估 style bias\n- 两层机制：(1) ~60% Likert ties 浪费评估预算 (2) absolute scoring 捕获弱于 forced comparison\n- 状态：✅ 5/6 cells confirmed (GPT-4o verbosity Likert ATE pending, pairwise 86.3% p<10⁻⁶)\n- 控制实验：binarized Likert sign test p=0.296 vs pairwise p=0.006 (exp-010) → 测量结构差异非统计检验差异\n- ordinal regression p=0.769 (exp-015) → 非 interval-scale assumption artifact\n- Power curve：binarized Likert 需 n≈462 才能 p<0.05（计入 tie rate），当前 n=88 严重 underpowered\n\n### C3 (Empirical — 跨轴跨模型 pattern): Style bias 的可检测性因 axis 语义性质而异\n- GEE decomposition gradient：Verbosity OR=13.10 (pure style, originality NS) > Formality OR=4.20/2.21 (mixed) > Register OR=1.91 (originality-dominated OR=5.72)\n- 方法边界：content-preserving axes (formality ✅, verbosity ✅) 可检测；改变认知承诺的 axes (tone ❌ NLI 65%) 结构性不兼容\n- 跨模型验证：GPT-4o vs Qwen3-32B, proprietary vs open-source, 相同方向\n\n### C4 (Practical): Practitioner guidance\n- Use pairwise over Likert for style bias audit\n- Per-axis decomposition reveals axis-specific confound structure (GEE gradient)\n- Content preservation verification per axis (direction-aware NLI for asymmetric axes)\n\n## Evidence Matrix (当前状态)\n\n| | GPT-4o | Qwen3-32B |\n|---|--------|-----------|\n| **Formality** | BT 63.0% [55.8, 70.3] p<0.001 ✅ Blindspot | BT 66.5% [58.5, 73.9] p<0.0001 ✅ Blindspot |\n| **Verbosity** | Pairwise 86.3% p<10⁻⁶ (**Likert ATE pending**) | BT 77.3% [70.3, 84.3] p<0.0001 ✅ Blindspot |\n| **Register** | 63.3% p=0.085 (NS, originality-dominated) | GEE OR=1.91 p=0.046 (exploratory) |\n\n**GEE Decomposition (Qwen3-32B)**:\n- Verbosity: style OR=13.10 p=2.6e-09, originality OR=0.49 p=0.096 (NS) → **confound-free**\n- Formality: style OR=4.20 p=0.0002, originality OR=4.70 p<0.0001 → **mixed**\n- Register: academic OR=1.91 p=0.046, originality OR=5.72 p<0.0001 → **originality-dominated**\n\n**GPT-4o GEE (formality only)**: formal OR=2.21 p=0.010, originality OR=1.82 p=0.052 (marginal)\n\n## Story Spine\n\n### Problem\nLLM-as-judge 是 NLP 评估和对齐训练的核心基础设施。Style bias 是主宰偏差（SOS-Bench R=0.999），但标准 Likert scoring 看不到它。\n\n### Existing Approaches & Their Gaps\n- **LC-AlpacaEval (ICLR'25)**: 回归控制 length bias，单维度，detection + correction\n- **SOS-Bench (ICLR'25)**: 注入缺陷量化 judge 敏感度，相关性分析非因果\n- **CASSE (2026)**: 12×12 style 矩阵，因果纠缠\n- **RATE (ICML'25)**: Double-rewrite ATE protocol — 用 Likert ATE → 本文证明 Likert 不敏感 → RATE 自身发现可能受 Likert Blindspot 影响（最强 positioning argument）\n- **Counterfactual Rhetorical (2025)**: persona counterfactual + BT aggregation，粒度不同\n- **Gap**: 无人系统性比较 Likert vs pairwise 在 style bias 检测中的 sensitivity gap；无人用 GEE decomposition 分离 style effect vs originality bias\n\n### Our Framing (Round 1 修正)\n用 binary style counterfactual + position-controlled pairwise comparison **interventionally measure** LLM judge 的 per-axis style bias。\n核心发现：**标准 Likert 评估系统性掩盖 style bias** — 在 5/6 judge×axis cells 中 pairwise 显著而 Likert 不显著。\nGEE decomposition 揭示 **跨轴 confound 梯度**，为 practitioner 提供 axis-specific bias 诊断。\n\n**语言规范**：\n- \"interventional\" / \"counterfactual-based measurement\"（非 \"causal\"）\n- DAG 已加入 §3.5（assumptions 段）\n- 全文已降调因果术语\n\n### Headline Result\n\"Standard Likert scoring declares no style bias, but position-controlled pairwise comparison on the same counterfactual data reveals significant style preference across 2 judges and 3 axes — this Likert Blindspot persists with BT win probabilities of 63-77% (all p<0.001) while Likert ATE remains non-significant.\"\n\n## Round 1 Review Issues — Resolution Status\n\n19 issues total (6 critical, 7 warning). Key resolution:\n\n**Effectively resolved**:\n- R1-W5 (post-hoc power): CI-based precision adopted, power curve reframed as illustrative\n- R1-W4 (multiple comparisons): Holm-Bonferroni family defined, primary/exploratory separation\n- CROSS-4 (ordinal regression): exp-015 p=0.769, Reviewer verified\n- R2-W2 (Bradley-Terry): BT as primary analysis, pair-level bootstrap\n\n**Near-resolved (writing patches in progress)**:\n- R1-N1 (causal language): 降调完成，DAG added\n- R1-N2 (NLI false-negative): Triple indirect evidence defense\n- R1-N3 (NLI threshold): Sensitivity analysis exp-011\n- R2-N1 (novelty): 2 judges × 3 axes with BT + GEE — Findings-level empirical value\n- R2-N3 (RATE criticism): h2h framing with BT upgrade\n- R2-W1 (scope): 2×3 matrix, 5/6 cells\n- R1-W1 (Likert baseline fairness): ordinal regression confirms Blindspot\n- R1-W2 (consistency filter): BT on all data rules out filter inflation\n\n**Gaps remaining**:\n- R2-N2 (references): 22 verified, reference audit done\n- R2-W4 (figures): Power curve ✅, Pipeline diagram ✅, Forest plot pending\n- R2-W3 (related work): Expanded to 5 paragraphs\n- CROSS-1 (efficiency gap framing): Two-layer mechanism, power curve shows n≈462 needed\n- Page count: Currently ~8.5 pages, compression in progress\n\n## Figures (3 planned)\n1. **Power curve** — ✅ Done. BT vs binarized Likert sensitivity comparison, with tie rate correction\n2. **Pipeline diagram** — ✅ Done. 5-stage CSD pipeline with attrition numbers\n3. **Forest plot** — ⏳ Pending. 2 judges × 3 axes BT win probabilities with 95% CI\n\n## Bibliography\n22 verified references (target: 25+). Key additions since Dream 2: DeCoster 2011, Hoenig 2001, Stevens 1946, Zeng 2024, Bradley & Terry 1952, Feinstein 1990.\n\n## Venue Fit\nEMNLP 2026 高度匹配。Round 1 得分 2.5 Borderline Findings，主要失分在写作质量（零图表、broken refs、page overflow）和 novelty framing。\n证据强度已满足 Findings 3.0-3.5 要求。Main 4.0 需要 novelty ceiling 突破（结构性限制，Likert Blindspot 是已知心理测量学现象的 domain transfer）。\n","numLines":118,"startLine":1,"totalLines":118}}}
